<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vere Bird</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1999">1999</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vere <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a> Bird was a trade unionist and politician who led Antigua from the 1950s. As chief minister and then premier of the self-governing colony, and from independence in 1981 the first prime minister of Antigua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a>, he dominated politics until 1994, when his son Lester succeeded him. His long rule was marked by allegations of corruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vere-bird.jpg" alt="Vere Bird" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pete Souza, White House · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vere_Bird_1986_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
